1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:09,069
The average scalp carries about a hundred
thousand follicles, each one pushing out
roughly zero point three millimetres of
hair every single day.

2
00:00:09,249 --> 00:00:15,774
That works out to about a centimetre each
month, which sounds tiny until you
remember it never stops until it does.

3
00:00:15,954 --> 00:00:24,951
A fingernail manages three and a half
metres in a lifetime, one strand reaches
nine, and every follicle on one head adds
up to nine kilometres a year.

4
00:00:25,131 --> 00:00:33,363
Over seventy five years that same scalp
grows seven hundred kilometres of hair,
two and a half times the drive from Delhi
to Jaipur.

5
00:00:33,543 --> 00:00:38,918
So your body measures time in millimetres,
so subscribe, and tap like.
